==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{m|frm|irrégularité}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|irregularitas}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|irregularities}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} An instance of being [[irregular]].
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The state or condition of being irregular, or the extent to which something is irregular.
# {{lb|en|countable}} An [[object]] or [[event]] that is not [[regular]] or [[ordinary]].
#: ''an '''irregularity''' of surface''
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[violation]] of rules.
#: ''An investigation of the '''irregularities''' in the company's accounts uncovered a large-scale fraud.''
# {{lb|en|euphemism}} Irregular bowel movement (e.g. [[diarrhea]] or [[constipation]]).
#* {{quote-book|author=James Dallas Jardine|author2=Indu Vaid|title=Alternative Therapies|publisher=Health Harmony|year=2000|isbn=8170218551|page=246|passage=Consuming copious amounts of vegetables, fruit, milk, and an abundance of water effectively treats '''irregularity'''. Establishing regular eating, bowel movement, and exercise habits are helpful too.}}

